caption: Addiction Penalty
technology-rule: addiction-penalty

The addiction penalty is:

Penalty = -ceil(BV / Addiction Divisor)

Round fractions up. Every chem therefore imposes at least Will-1.

| Benefit Value relative to divisor | Will roll |
| --- | --- |
| Up to 1 divisor | Will-1 |
| Over 1 and up to 2 divisors | Will-2 |
| Over 2 and up to 3 divisors | Will-3 |
| Over 3 and up to 4 divisors | Will-4 |

On a failed roll, the character becomes addicted to that exact chem formula.

An addiction to an integrated chem is an addiction to the entire integrated state. Its individual effects do not satisfy the addiction separately.

Separate chems create separate possible addictions.

Once a character is already addicted to a formula, further doses do not require additional rolls to acquire the same addiction. Use the normal campaign rules for maintaining and overcoming Addiction.
